# Lazy-load closed UI

A dialog, chart, or other widget the user opens only sometimes stays out of the file-manager startup chunk.

- Load it with `lazy(() => import(...))` from the shell (`FileManagerPage`).
- Render it only while its open flag is true, inside `<Suspense fallback={null}>`.
- Skip it while the editor workspace is open, unless it belongs to the editor.
- A heavy library (a chart, a treemap, CodeMirror) is imported from that dialog file, so opening the dialog is what downloads it. Do not import it from a store, the toolbar, the command palette, or the page module.
- The menu or shortcut only sets the open flag.

```tsx
const TreemapDialog = lazy(() =>
  import('../../widgets/disk-treemap/TreemapDialog').then((m) => ({ default: m.TreemapDialog })),
);

{treemapOpen && !editorOpen && (
  <Suspense fallback={null}>
    <TreemapDialog />
  </Suspense>
)}
```
